            // that read history now would read the reply as intended rather than
            // as heard. The wait is bounded by this turn's own abandonment, and a
            // correction that outlives a confirmed turn waiting on it has had its
            // window: the next turn does not wait on it again, so a hook that
            // never settles costs one turn, not the call. A guess that waits and
            // is refined hands the wait to what replaces it (see `#interrupt`).
